# 11-terraform-modules.md

# Terraform Modules

> **Sprint:** 3 – Infrastructure as Code (IaC)
> **Status:** ✅ Completed

---

# Overview

Terraform Modules are reusable collections of Terraform resources that help organize infrastructure into smaller, maintainable components.

In this project, separate modules are used for:

- VPC
- Amazon EKS

---

# Why Use Modules?

- Reusable code
- Cleaner project structure
- Easier maintenance
- Better scalability
- Reduced duplication

---

# Project Structure

```text
terraform/
├── modules/
│   ├── vpc/
│   └── eks/
└── environments/
```

---

# Benefits

- Easy to reuse
- Simplifies infrastructure management
- Supports multiple environments

---

# Best Practices

- One module for one responsibility
- Use variables and outputs
- Avoid duplicate code

---

# Interview Questions

- What is a Terraform Module?
- Why use modules instead of one large file?
- What are module inputs and outputs?

---

# Summary

Terraform Modules improve code organization, reusability, and scalability by separating infrastructure into reusable components.

