# 12-vpc.md

# Amazon VPC

> **Sprint:** 3 – Infrastructure as Code (IaC)
> **Status:** ✅ Completed

---

# Overview

Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) provides an isolated network for AWS resources.

The VPC created in this project is used to host the Amazon EKS cluster securely.

---

# Components

- VPC
- Public Subnets
- Private Subnets
- Internet Gateway
- NAT Gateway
- Route Tables

---

# Architecture

```text
Internet
    │
Internet Gateway
    │
Public Subnets
    │
NAT Gateway
    │
Private Subnets
    │
Amazon EKS
```

---

# Why Private Subnets?

- Improved security
- Worker nodes are not directly exposed to the internet
- Internet access through NAT Gateway

---

# Best Practices

- Use multiple Availability Zones
- Keep workloads in private subnets
- Enable least-privilege networking

---

# Interview Questions

- What is a VPC?
- Difference between public and private subnets?
- Why use a NAT Gateway?

---

# Summary

The VPC provides a secure networking foundation for deploying Kubernetes clusters and other AWS resources.
