# 13-eks.md

# Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (EKS)

> **Sprint:** 3 – Infrastructure as Code (IaC)
> **Status:** ✅ Completed

---

# Overview

Amazon EKS is a managed Kubernetes service that simplifies deploying and operating Kubernetes clusters on AWS.

In this project, Terraform is used to provision the EKS cluster.

---

# EKS Components

- Control Plane (Managed by AWS)
- Worker Nodes
- Node Groups
- IAM Roles
- VPC Networking

---

# Architecture

```text
Developer
    │
Terraform
    │
Amazon EKS
    │
Worker Nodes
    │
Containers
```

---

# Why EKS?

- Managed Kubernetes
- High availability
- Automatic control plane management
- Easy AWS integration

---

# Benefits

- Scalable
- Secure
- Production-ready
- Supports Kubernetes ecosystem

---

# Best Practices

- Deploy worker nodes in private subnets
- Use IAM Roles for Service Accounts (IRSA)
- Provision infrastructure using Terraform

---

# Interview Questions

- What is Amazon EKS?
- Why use EKS instead of self-managed Kubernetes?
- What components make up an EKS cluster?

---

# Summary

Amazon EKS provides a fully managed Kubernetes control plane, allowing engineers to focus on deploying and managing applications instead of maintaining Kubernetes infrastructure.